<title>PERU: Peru net intl reserves rise to $8.962 bln Dec 18.</title>
<headline>Peru net intl reserves rise to $8.962 bln Dec 18.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves rose to $8.962 billion on December 18 from $8.563 billion a week earlier.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short- and long-term debt obligations, was $1.709 billion on December 18.</p>
<p>President Alberto Fujimori said earlier last month the government expected Peru's international reserves to rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
